  "claim": "Henson Airlines Flight 1517 crashed at an airport in Virginia. This airport and airport built on the former site of the Marine Corps Air Station Santa Barbara are both in the United States.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport. Sentence: Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport (IATA: SHD, ICAO: KSHD, FAA LID: SHD) is a public airport located 10 nautical miles (12 mi, 19 km) northeast of the central business district of Staunton, a city in Augusta County, Virginia, United States.\nPage: Santa Barbara Municipal Airport. Sentence: Santa Barbara Municipal Airport (IATA: SBA, ICAO: KSBA, FAA LID: SBA) is a public airport 7 mi west of downtown Santa Barbara, California, United States.\nPage: Henson Airlines Flight 1517. Sentence: On September 23, 1985, Henson Airlines Flight 1517 crashed in Grottoes, Virginia, while on approach to the Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport.\nPage: Marine Corps Air Station Santa Barbara. Sentence: Following the surrender of Japan and the subsequent drawdown of forces that ensued, the air station closed its doors in 1946 and today its property is home to the Santa Barbara Municipal Airport and the campus of the University of California, Santa Barbara.",
