        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport, Santa Barbara Municipal Airport, Staunton, Augusta County, Virginia, Santa Barbara, California, Grottoes, University of California, Santa Barbara\n- Organizations: Henson Airlines, Marine Corps Air Station Santa Barbara\n- Events: Henson Airlines Flight 1517 crash, post-World War II military drawdown\n\nFacts:\n- In 1946, Marine Corps Air Station Santa Barbara closed following Japan’s surrender and the subsequent military drawdown.\n- The former property of Marine Corps Air Station Santa Barbara is now home to Santa Barbara Municipal Airport and the campus of the University of California, Santa Barbara.\n- On September 23, 1985, Henson Airlines Flight 1517 crashed in Grottoes, Virginia, while on approach to Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport.\n- Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport is a public airport located 10 nautical miles northeast of the central business district of Staunton in Augusta County, Virginia, United States.\n- Santa Barbara Municipal Airport is a public airport located 7 miles west of downtown Santa Barbara, California, United States.",
